---
alwaysApply: true
---
- After creating a GitHub PR, create a follow-up commit with a CHANGELOG.md entry with a single-sentence description of the change. Add new entries only under `## [Unreleased]`, using one of these subsections: Added, Changed, Deprecated, Removed, Fixed, or Security. Create the subsection under `Unreleased` if it does not exist, and place the new entry at the bottom of that subsection. End the entry with the GitHub pull request link formatted as `[#<id>](https://github.com/sourcebot-dev/sourcebot/pull/<id>)` (e.g., `[#696](https://github.com/sourcebot-dev/sourcebot/pull/696)`). Never add entries under a released version header such as `## [x.y.z] - YYYY-MM-DD`, move or rewrite unrelated existing entries, or place the new entry anywhere else.
- When creating a GitHub PR for a given issue, always include "Fixes #<id>" in the body of the GitHub PR description, where <id> is the id of the GitHub issue.